{
  "title": "A Prospective Cohort Study on Hyponatremia in Preterm Neonates",
  "publication_date": "2023-04-17T00:00:00Z",
  "summary": "A medical research study comparing sodium measurement methods in premature newborns, specifically examining the differences between blood gas analyzers and laboratory autoanalyzers in detecting hyponatremia.",
  "content": "The study investigated the measurement of sodium levels in preterm neonates using different analytical methods. The research compared readings from blood gas analyzers and laboratory autoanalyzers to determine their accuracy and reliability in diagnosing hyponatremia in premature babies. The investigation was conducted as a prospective cohort study, highlighting the importance of accurate sodium measurement in neonatal care.\n\nThe research aimed to improve the diagnostic accuracy of hyponatremia in preterm infants, as proper sodium level management is crucial for their development and survival. The findings contribute to better understanding of measurement methodologies in neonatal intensive care units.",
